              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.3: A 15-cm scale"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.225,
            0.511,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of 1 cm length are further divided into 10 equal parts. The length of one of these smaller parts is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "millimetre",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "mm",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "). 1 mm is the smallest value of length that you can measure using this scale. 1 mm is equal to one-tenth of a centimeter (1 mm = 0.1 cm)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.39,
            0.494,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For measuring larger lengths, we use a larger unit called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "kilometre",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "km",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ") which is equal to 1000 metres. And for measuring smaller lengths, we use units such as centimetre or millimetre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.549,
            0.279,
            0.864,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Would it be convenient to use the unit metre to measure larger lengths, such as the length of a railway track between two cities, or to measure smaller lengths, such as the thickness of a page of a book?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.542,
            0.305,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 km = 1000 m"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.542,
            0.505,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 m = 100 cm"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.543,
            0.716,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 cm = 10 mm",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.619,
            0.757,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In some scales, you might have noticed another scale marking. This scale marking is in inches, where 1 inch = 2.54 cm. In earlier days, units, such as inch and foot, were used to measure length. These units are still used by some people."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
